# Response headers for the deployed SPA. Cloudflare Pages reads this file from the root of
# what it publishes (public/ is copied into dist/ verbatim by Vite); after the on-prem
# move Workers Static Assets reads the same file. Matching is order-sensitive and MERGED:
# /* carries the security headers, and the asset rule below only adds Cache-Control.
#
# ONE POLICY FOR DEV AND PROD — a static file cannot specialise per environment. The
# localhost entries the old index.html <meta> CSP carried (Garage on localhost:4620, the
# API on localhost:3000) are dev-only and deliberately GONE: local `pnpm dev` runs without
# a CSP, and the deployed dev environment talks to the same origins as prod — same-origin
# API through the edge (Pages Functions proxy today, no-Worker routes after the move) and
# R2 presigned attachments.
#
# *.r2.cloudflarestorage.com is required for attachments: uploads go DIRECTLY from the
# browser via a presigned PUT, and downloads follow a 302 to a presigned GET, so both
# connect-src and img-src need it. rova-assets{-dev}.qnsc.vn are the PUBLIC-asset origins
# (avatars, workspace logos), img-src ONLY — a custom domain replaces the r2 host entirely,
# so the wildcard does not cover it. They are named explicitly because a *.qnsc.vn wildcard
# would let any future subdomain serve images into the app.
#
# connect-src blob: covers the rich-text paste preview (createObjectURL, then fetch of the
# blob URL before upload); worker-src blob: covers workers constructed from inline blobs.
#
# script-src has NO 'unsafe-inline': the built index.html carries no inline script (Vite
# emits module scripts by URL). The Entra redirect is a full-page NAVIGATION, never a
# fetch, so login.microsoftonline.com / login.microsoft.com / graph.microsoft.com appear
# nowhere in connect-src — the SPA holds no tokens and calls no Microsoft API directly.
# Google Fonts is gone from style/font-src: the app renders no Google Fonts (kept only
# by inertia from the old meta). form-action keeps login.microsoftonline.com: the SSO
# redirect POSTs a form there.
#
# frame-ancestors and X-Frame-Options are here, as HEADERS — neither does anything in a
# <meta> tag, which is why they were never in the removed one.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; font-src 'self' data:; img-src 'self' data: blob: https://*.r2.cloudflarestorage.com https://rova-assets-dev.qnsc.vn https://rova-assets.qnsc.vn; connect-src 'self' blob: https://*.r2.cloudflarestorage.com; worker-src blob:; base-uri 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; form-action 'self' https://login.microsoftonline.com;
  Cache-Control: no-cache

# Content-hashed filenames: the bytes behind a given URL never change.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
